*ONFLY probe 3a of 3 (D-129): a BMS mapset, the BUZZ menu in miniature.
*
*Section 3.7 says BUZZ "will be a menu transaction (BMS screen) that
*lets the user pick a stimulus, rate, duration and seed".  This is that
*screen cut down to two fields, because the question is not whether the
*menu is complete but whether BMS exists at all under Raincode's QIX.
*
*BMS maps are assembler macros and have to be assembled twice: once as
*TYPE=MAP to produce the physical map the terminal server uses, and once
*as TYPE=DSECT to produce the symbolic map ONFCMAP.cbl copies.  Whether
*Raincode ships anything that can do that is exactly what this probe
*asks.  If it does not, D-127's 3270 half needs another route and
*ONFCTRM's SEND TEXT is the fallback.
*
*Continuation is column 72, operands resume in column 16.  Verified
*mechanically rather than by eye - see the README.
*
ONFCMS   DFHMSD TYPE=&SYSPARM,MODE=INOUT,LANG=COBOL,STORAGE=AUTO,      X
               TIOAPFX=YES,CTRL=(FREEKB,ALARM)
ONFCMP   DFHMDI SIZE=(24,80)
         DFHMDF POS=(1,1),LENGTH=17,ATTRB=(PROT,BRT),                  X
               INITIAL='ONFLY - BUZZ menu'
         DFHMDF POS=(3,1),LENGTH=11,ATTRB=(PROT),INITIAL='Stimulus :'
STIMC    DFHMDF POS=(3,14),LENGTH=8,ATTRB=(UNPROT,IC)
         DFHMDF POS=(3,23),LENGTH=1,ATTRB=(PROT)
         DFHMDF POS=(4,1),LENGTH=11,ATTRB=(PROT),INITIAL='Rate Hz  :'
RATEF    DFHMDF POS=(4,14),LENGTH=4,ATTRB=(UNPROT)
         DFHMDF POS=(4,19),LENGTH=1,ATTRB=(PROT)
MSGF     DFHMDF POS=(6,1),LENGTH=60,ATTRB=(PROT,BRT)
         DFHMSD TYPE=FINAL
         END
